# The scripts and the harness run under WSL2 / Linux. Without this, a clone on
# Windows with core.autocrlf=true gets CRLF line endings and every shell script
# fails with "bad interpreter".
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf

# Results CSVs are left exactly as the harness wrote them. Python's csv module
# emits RFC 4180 CRLF line endings; normalising those would make every file
# show as modified the moment a run is repeated.
*.csv -text
